# Firmware backlog

Before starting Astrolabe firmware work:

1. Read [`docs/BACKLOG.md`](docs/BACKLOG.md) and pick or confirm the active item.
2. Ensure a **GitHub issue** exists (create from [Feature](../.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/feature.yml) / [Bugfix](../.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bugfix.yml) templates if missing). Follow [`docs/WORKFLOW.md`](docs/WORKFLOW.md).
3. Work on branch `feature/<#>-slug` or `fix/<#>-slug` from **`integration`** (Cursor Cloud: branch from the issue).
4. Mark backlog `[~]` under **In progress** with `Issue: #N` (keep 1–3 items there).

When finishing a **feature** (backlog item):

1. If it adds or changes a **clock face**, run the **hardware QA loop** in [hardware-qa.mdc](hardware-qa.mdc): upload (or JTAG inject face) → `screen.bmp` screenshot → evaluate before marking done.
2. Mark it `[x]` and move it to **Done** with `YYYY-MM-DD` and **PR / issue** link (`Closes #N`).
3. Open or update **PR** against **`integration`**; merge when CI green (agents: see [integration-branch.mdc](integration-branch.mdc)). Promote to **`main`** only after flash QA.
4. **Commit before the next feature** — see [git-workflow.mdc](git-workflow.mdc) and [github-workflow.mdc](github-workflow.mdc).
5. Only then pick up the next backlog item (new issue + branch).

When finishing a session (partial work):

1. Leave **In progress** accurate.
2. Offer a checkpoint commit if the diff is large or the next session will tackle a different feature.

Other:

- Design context stays in [`docs/pocketwatch.md`](docs/pocketwatch.md); do not duplicate long specs in the backlog.
